  "journal": {
    "s14_sunspire_records": {
      "title": "The Sunspire Records",
      "text": "Sunspire, the capital of Solkar, stands round a tower older than the city itself. Sahir met us at the House of Records. An old survey mentions a circle beneath six landmarks, one for each civilisation, and the stacks gave us the old names of three of them. We decoded a Builder inscription: 'Open the circle only in its hour.' A water-stained page spoke of a deep note that holds the world in time. The survey's central mark may be the northern monument, but only as one part of something larger. On the great map six lines met near Awakening Valley. The sealed crate our caravan saved was bound for Sahir's house: Solkar's piece. Sahir is coming with us. Lord Kaelen of Emberhold has refused every letter, so we will ask him in person."
    }
  }
}